  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Monday...\n\nShowers and thunderstorms are expected across Southeast Montana \ntoday and Tuesday. Showers and thunderstorms will get started this\nafternoon over the western high terrain and move to the east \nthroughout the evening before coming to an end by midnight. \nIsolated severe storms will bring the threat for wind gusts in \nexcess of 60 mph. Tuesday will also see showers and thunderstorms \ndevelop in the afternoon with showers lasting through the \novernight till around 6 AM Wednesday. Temperatures Tuesday will be\na couple of degrees cooler than today with temperatures in the \n80s F. \n\nEnsemble systems are in good agreement that upper-level \nridging will begin to build over the region Wednesday through \nSaturday. This will cause temperatures to increase into the 90s F \nfor most locations Thursday through Saturday. Starting Friday, \nupper-level ridging will allow southwest moisture to advect into \nthe region bringing a monsoon pattern. This will act to increase \nprecipitation chances through the weekend. Early next week, above \naverage upper-level heights remain but upper-level ridging weakens\ntaking a few degrees off temperatures. Torgerson",
